Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: restore original direction after fullcone lookup

Backport the tuple-direction correction from openwrt-sonic-fullcone:
https://github.com/mufeng05/openwrt-sonic-fullcone/commit/e5cbaad43fe15c8f879a0f456b448d578c0eac4d

nf_ct_invert_tuple() leaves dst.dir at REPLY. Restore ORIGINAL before
returning the inbound tuple so replies receive NAT. Retain OWRT's locking,
isolated reservations and flowtable/PPE integration unchanged.

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_nat_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_nat_core.c
@@ -646,6 +646,10 @@ find_appropriate_dst(struct net *net,
 			nf_ct_invert_tuple(result,
 					   &ct->tuplehash[IP_CT_DIR_ORIGINAL].tuple);
 			result->src = tuple->src;
+			/* nf_ct_invert_tuple() set dir to REPLY, but result
+			 * is an original-direction tuple.
+			 */
+			result->dst.dir = IP_CT_DIR_ORIGINAL;
 			found = 1;
 			break;
 		}
